---
title: Clients and contacts
description: Keep track of who you bill and the people you deal with there.
---

## Clients

A client is a company or a person you send invoices to. Go to **Billing → Clients** and choose **Create a client**.

- **Type**: **Company** or **Individual**.
- **Name**: the only required field.
- **VAT number**: if the client has one, in the form `CHE-123.456.789 MWST`.
- **Address**: printed on your invoices.
- **Communication**: **Language**, **Email**, **Phone** and **Website**.

{% aside type="tip" %}
Fill in the full address, street, postal code, city and country. The QR-bill only includes the
payer when it's complete. And set the client's **Language**: invoices are prepared in it by
default.
{% /aside %}

## Contacts

Contacts are the people you deal with at a client: the managing director, someone in accounting, and so on. Open a client and choose **Add contact** to record their **First name**, **Last name**, **Email** and **Phone**.

Contacts are for your own reference. They don't appear on invoices.

## Deleting

Deleting a client also deletes its contacts. A client you've already invoiced can't be deleted, so your books stay complete.
